 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request sends `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are kept in the data
+as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- `viewer` may only read (`GET`).
+- `cook` may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager` may do everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a known key without
+permission answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than `GET` made with a known key writes an audit entry
+`{ "at", "keyName", "method", "path", "status" }`, whatever its outcome.
+`GET /audit` lists the entries newest first (managers only).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
